  "notes": "Closed-score SATB: Soprano+Alto share the treble staff, Tenor+Bass share the bass staff. A correct conversion yields FOUR parts (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass), each with its own notes; all three verses belong to the Soprano part (lyric numbers 1-3) and must stay attached to soprano notes, including melisma skips (e.g. \"pre - cious\" spans a slurred melisma). DAMAGE (stain-pencil): Rehearsal copy: coffee ring stains (scan: one ring over the music), graphite pencil marks - circled notes, handwritten words (\"rit.\", \"breathe\", \"p\", \"cresc.\" ...), breath ticks/commas, arrows, phrase arcs. Severe adds three stains, yellow and pink highlighter over staff passages, blue ballpoint circles/words and margin scribbles. Exact positions of every mark are listed per file in meta.annotations. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Handwritten marks (including handwritten dynamics such as \"p\", \"mf\", \"cresc.\", \"rit.\" and fingerings) are NOT in the truth: the truth only contains the engraved music. A conversion that adds them as dynamics/words/fingerings is wrong for scoring purposes."
 },
